---
<DocsLayout title="A place for every feature." section="architecture" summary="LunaDash keeps its Wayland compositor, desktop services and shell in clear source domains, with build checks that protect those boundaries.">
  <h2 id="runtime">How the desktop fits together</h2>
  <p>The C++20 compositor uses wlroots for Wayland protocols, input and scene output. Quickshell runs the QML shell in a separate process. Native tools use Qt Widgets, and the file chooser portal exposes a D-Bus service. The compositor does not use Qt Wayland Compositor or implement an X11 window manager.</p>
  <p>XWayland remains an authenticated compatibility container that starts on demand. The refactor preserves the existing window animations, wlroots version compatibility, configuration paths and command-line executable names.</p>
  <h2 id="domains">Find the feature you want to change</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Under src/</th><th scope="col">Responsibility</th></tr></thead><tbody>{domains.map(([name, description]) => <tr><th scope="row"><code>{name}/</code></th><td>{description}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Directories use lowercase names. Adjacent C++ interfaces and implementations use PascalCase <code>.hpp</code> and <code>.cpp</code> files in the <code>LunaDash</code> namespace. Each executable has a small <code>Main.cpp</code>; its startup logic belongs to its application module. C functions retain the <code>ludash_</code> prefix.</p>
  <h2 id="rendering">Rendering has an explicit owner</h2>
  <p><code>compositor/renderer/</code> contains rendering orchestration. Raw OpenGL implementation, resource owners and built-in GLSL live together under <code>renderer/opengl/</code>. CMake embeds the shaders into the binary, so installed applications never need the source checkout or a particular working directory.</p>
  <p>The active compositor uses the wlroots scene renderer. The retained Qt OpenGL element library is compiled and tested separately; its blur and procedural wallpaper passes are not currently connected to that scene. Image wallpaper and shell transitions are supplied by Quickshell.</p>
  <h2 id="extend">Add a feature without spreading its details</h2>
  <ol><li>Choose the owning domain and define its public interface.</li><li>Make lifetime ownership explicit; use the existing module, feature and listener contracts where they help.</li><li>List sources in the owning CMake target and keep implementation resources with their module.</li><li>Update tests, the technical documentation and the matching website guide.</li></ol>
  <p>Core code cannot include higher-level domains. Desktop services cannot include compositor internals, and renderer code cannot include desktop UI. CI rejects invalid include directions, naming violations, unlisted source files and misplaced GL code.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="ARCHITECTURE AND REGRESSION CHECKS" code={'python3 scripts/check-source-layout.py\npython3 tests/architecture/test_source_layout.py\ncmake -S . -B build -G Ninja \\\n  -DLUDASH_BUILD_FILES_TESTS=ON -DLUDASH_BUILD_RENDERER_TESTS=ON\ncmake --build build --parallel 2\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure'} />
  <h2 id="verification">What passing checks establish</h2>
  <p>The workflows cover source structure, builds, file operations, embedded shader loading and cleanup, software OpenGL, wlroots protocol and window lifecycles, Qt clients, on-demand XWayland and this website. The source-build matrix configures Arch, Debian, Fedora, openSUSE and Alpine jobs. Always inspect the completed runs for the exact commit before claiming a platform passed.</p>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>LunaDash remains a development preview.</strong> Physical GPUs, display-manager login, multiple outputs, Chrome/Zed and full input-method behavior need session testing. Screen locking and a complete PipeWire screen-sharing portal are not implemented. Native plugins remain opt-in and execute without a sandbox.</p></div>
  <p>Read the <a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash/blob/dev/docs/en/ARCHITECTURE.md">technical architecture</a> and <a href="https://github.com/LuYishan-4/LunaDash/blob/dev/docs/en/TESTING_AND_FILES.md">testing and source map</a> for ownership details and the current validation commands.</p>
</DocsLayout>
